#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bf932ea-d614-5105-b448-3e3b99454b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}x^3+2x^2+x+e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600579} :answer-field/id #uuid "2deddd47-ba64-5f9b-aab1-cc17a575d553" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5920d0ed-6eed-52ea-b84d-149008f70600" :question/math-academy-id "q-167775" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\n$${{field-1}}\n$+C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "We combine the sum and the constant multiple rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+{e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5e0a8de-219b-5898-bd70-722e7611ca94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600697}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600697} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e25b0a3-6334-5613-a916-5f4c7ed6f7c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c4ebeef6-ac1c-5e75-b469-0c94d4213e5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167772" :question/problem "Given that $y=h(g(x)),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,=8(\\,$\n{{field-1}}$)\\,{e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $y$ is a composite function:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{s},\\,s=2g=2(2{x}^{2}+4x+1)=4{x}^{2}+8x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}={e}^{s},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=8x+8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{s}\\cdot (8x+8) \\\\  & =8(x+1){e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55139606-5928-55a4-b814-22a969ada28b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6t(t^2+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601654}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601654} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc71457a-ed2e-5826-8272-b8f37053afd2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c125870a-b46c-59e0-a9be-37ea8a9a1d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-132994" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[({t}^{2}+1)^{3}]=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's define a function $h(t):$\n\n$$\nh(t)=({t}^{2}+1)^{3}\n$$\n\nTo differentiate this function, we use the chain rule. Let \n\n$$\ng(t)={t}^{2}+1,\\,h(g(t))=g(t)^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating our functions, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =({t}^{2}+1)^{′}=2t, \\\\ {h}^{′}(g(t)) & =({g}^{3})^{′}=3{g}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[({t}^{2}+1)^{3}] & ={h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={h}^{′}(g(t))\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =3{g}^{2}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =6t({t}^{2}+1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8de825b3-d8e3-5f00-bdfa-5a4cd69a0f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sin x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608639} :answer-field/id #uuid "6214df7d-9285-5717-a4db-91deee6effb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "90b2fc35-232b-52fe-83ab-e606cc458425" :question/math-academy-id "q-352076" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\pi )=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(\\pi )=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +C \\\\ 1 & =4(0)+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c9743c-696b-5e98-9bc8-e13ae1a9170e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/31/31bd6e2544b5a09dcd8cf55d01120cc2e50a885486ef49b08755ef0ddd439fba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608490} {:answer/id #uuid "8e968a93-133a-58cf-a9cd-3cc6df1fed62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6e/6e09fcdeada8df3bd52b0a1660ba42289d9dcaa1a1dea7a121a3b5ace6beb35e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608642} {:answer/id #uuid "b3dfeb46-7382-509f-b820-e5843341fd26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8c/8c97eee4c68abd7ead403b8e9cc0f6bb8a7436d750959b8363fa0dd2cc033cca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608715} {:answer/id #uuid "bd775b54-2938-5a0b-890c-7ed59c033cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ec/ec302f8524fb77cef46254807c20797855eab4674c30a8246f364b950f14a76f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608728} {:answer/id #uuid "be5d731e-e7c0-5f10-b9ba-c6ff3d9ea4ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/41/41298a40db8b8c945a90fb1524121da39a75efad85396e16f5e42480a9bb503a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608730}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608642} :answer-field/id #uuid "f046d02d-53f4-57ae-9a87-6ed2adc06e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9b13931e-9102-5325-a68f-f7705e245c4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-119137" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-3,0,3.$\n\n![](images/f7/f725d451c75aeb39d10c66d6e640abd432f25bd0df8779f55d0ac8512993a139.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2adf94cb-7729-58d4-8793-1c388aa09662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{2+6x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608492} {:answer/id #uuid "9387ef1a-4ba5-57ee-8855-974c04fb7687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{2x+3+K}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608650} {:answer/id #uuid "a47bc7e5-4700-5718-8711-560af91dd168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+3x+K}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608681} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eac54b-c2a3-5fd1-ad57-3948ea949514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608685} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d63037-846d-55fb-ad22-48cbc1f061ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x+K}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608740}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608740} :answer-field/id #uuid "991e65cc-3f69-5d2f-904a-a7052482fcc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9faaedf3-7c41-5002-95a6-335a2235c1fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-14251" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2x+3}{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{2x+3}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x+3}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={x}^{2}+3x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}={x}^{2}+3x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={x}^{2}+3x+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2{x}^{2}+6x+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186609013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002df87b-961d-5d8f-8186-916f1e10a70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}e^{-3x}+\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608428}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608428} :answer-field/id #uuid "306df2f6-0d41-5fe7-84bf-69f0243c7983" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e84e20f1-1924-5f17-9507-878a96060fea" :question/math-academy-id "q-347844" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}+{e}^{-3x}=6x+2$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y=3{x}^{2}+2x+\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=6x+2-{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6x+2-{e}^{-3x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (6x+2)\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+2x)-\\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=3{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3(0)^{2}+2(0)+\\frac{{e}^{-3(0)}}{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =0+0+\\frac{1}{3}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=3{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6156880b-52c6-5bdc-9c2e-214c28010017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 10 e^{- 6 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610448} {:answer/id #uuid "85f39285-5979-5f26-9c13-6279224ea917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 6 e^{- 6 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610453} {:answer/id #uuid "d54d8ce4-0272-5122-8b5f-d147266f1933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 e^{- 6 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610464} {:answer/id #uuid "ee874359-fc83-5033-bc87-1079cd37b759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 e^{- 6 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610467} {:answer/id #uuid "f1580a99-076a-5df3-9a20-6df72ad588ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12 e^{- 6 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610468} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1261795-f79c-5f9c-9108-fe798e6e4bd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0864cf01-5370-55e0-a300-a4fb8f259792" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=-2{e}^{-6x-4}+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=-2{e}^{u}+2,\\,u=-6x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-2{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =12{e}^{u} \\\\  & =12{e}^{-6x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c5e447-89e7-5391-a098-c71461de5b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 9 e^{2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610445} {:answer/id #uuid "84c8ec94-a775-5f7e-b54a-2ea5e7208145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 12 e^{2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610452} {:answer/id #uuid "b46d18df-a44a-5341-a49a-344afbfe2174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 6 e^{2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610459} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb30be3-47ae-5546-979f-4e0f2b801fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18 e^{2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610461} {:answer/id #uuid "e751ff94-b294-52bd-9fa4-915e8d14a319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 e^{2 x - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610459} :answer-field/id #uuid "01612884-385b-5594-af4f-0fd4fdfd5daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "222af1dd-8c2b-5df0-87c0-f198b956462a" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=-3{e}^{2x-4}+8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=-3{e}^{u}+8,\\,u=2x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-3{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-6{e}^{2x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f4e93c-5746-5e9a-bc0a-47985096bbf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 3 e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610443} {:answer/id #uuid "7826582c-cdbb-5dac-ade4-dea0796046a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610450} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b23144-1d29-51a6-8624-78b3844d0519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb